    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Stub .sys with spoofed 'Capcom Co., Ltd.' vendor metadata dropped to user TEMP", "technique": "T1211", "what_happened": "At 2032-09-29 15:18:08 UTC, Sysmon EID 11 reports powershell.exe creating C:\\Users\\r.morrison\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\p97_t02_151808\\capcom_stub_151808.sys (2048 bytes). File header is MZ + minimal PE stub. Custom rule 200304 triggered.", "chain_reason": "Stub .sys in user TEMP with vendor-string spoofing ('Capcom Co., Ltd.') mimics the legitimate Capcom.sys driver historically abused for kernel R/W primitives in CVE-2016-7986."},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "sc.exe create with type=kernel and DisplayName='Capcom Sys'", "technique": "T1543.003", "what_happened": "At 2032-09-29 15:18:12, Sysmon EID 1 captures sc.exe with cmdline 'sc.exe create p97_capcom_151808 binPath= C:\\Users\\...\\capcom_stub_151808.sys type= kernel start= demand DisplayName= Capcom Sys 151808'. Custom rule 200300 + Security EID 4697 triggered.", "chain_reason": "The DisplayName 'Capcom Sys' is another spoofing signal — attackers use vendor-evocative names so a quick service-list audit looks legitimate."},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "sc start invocation on the new kernel service", "technique": "T1211", "what_happened": "At 2032-09-29 15:18:15, Sysmon EID 1 captures sc.exe with cmdline 'sc.exe start p97_capcom_151808'. Whether the kernel image is actually mapped depends on Driver Signature Enforcement — the stub is not validly signed.", "chain_reason": "sc start logs the load attempt regardless of whether DSE permits it; Sysmon EID 6 will tell us if the load succeeded."},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Sysmon EID 6 (Driver loaded) — kernel-load confirmation event", "technique": "T1211", "what_happened": "At 2032-09-29 15:18:17, Sysmon EID 6 may or may not fire depending on DSE / Code Integrity. If it fires with imageLoaded matching the stub AND signed=false, the kernel was actually mapped with attacker-controlled code.", "chain_reason": "EID 6 is the definitive kernel-load evidence; its presence or absence is the dividing line between 'attempted BYOVD' and 'successful BYOVD with ring-0 capability'."}
  ],
